=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play engine/best-effort-ubuntu2204 ---------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: engine/best-effort-ubuntu2204$
# web-01.example.net runs Ubuntu 22.04, a best-effort release:$
# hardn changes it, but is not tested on it. sshd listens on$
# port 22, and ufw is active, allowing 22/tcp.$
# The plan alone, for key-only login: it carries the release's$
# warning (P-41).$
$
  [ ] Ubuntu 22.04 is a best-effort release: its vendor still$
      supports it and hardn changes it, but hardn is not tested$
      on it$
$
   -  Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service$
      @@ -0,0 +1,23 @@$
      +# hardn's boot unit (P-34 (c);$
      | docs/safety/revert-boot.md). hardn installs$
      +# it before it arms the revert timer of a change that$
      | could lock you out, and$
      +# removes it at a boot that finds no change journalled.$
      +#$
      +# At boot, before sshd reads its files: re-arm the revert$
      | timer of a change$
      +# waiting for "hardn confirm", for what remains of its$
      | window, or roll the$
      +# change back when its deadline has passed. Ordering$
      | only: sshd starts$
      +# whatever this unit does.$
      +[Unit]$
      +Description=hardn: re-arm or run the revert timer of an$
      | unconfirmed change$
      +DefaultDependencies=no$
      +After=local-fs.target sysinit.target ufw.service$
      +Before=ssh.service ssh.socket shutdown.target$
      +Conflicts=shutdown.target$
      +$
      +[Service]$
      +Type=oneshot$
      +RemainAfterExit=yes$
      +ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/hardn rollback --boot$
      +TimeoutStartSec=7min$
      +$
      +[Install]$
      +WantedBy=multi-user.target$
      -not installed$
      +installed and enabled$
      $ systemd-analyze verify --recursive-errors=no$
      | /run/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx/hardn-boot.service$
      $ systemctl --no-reload enable hardn-boot.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Disallow password login$
$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,4 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn.$
      +# Set by hardn:$
      +PasswordAuthentication no$
      +KbdInteractiveAuthentication no$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
$
      ssh.service$
      $ systemctl reload ssh.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      sshd -T shows no password login$
$
      sshd -T$
      $ sshd -T$
$
  No actual changes were made to your system.$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

